    "q-80708": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80708",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14223512/assets/32165a622d57d6af278b7ce288093ef4db6867619046b8625071f0274a1c7e93.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nI. ${y}^{′}={x}^{3}y+{x}^{3}$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}=xy-x$\n\nIII. ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14223512/assets/a278676af009b7096bd50f9b3918f0e8090c1822a9e029ac2b4b6325d1ba7a4c.png)\n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- First, the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the lines $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on both of these lines.\n\n- Second, the lines $x=0$ and $y=-1$ divide the plane into $4$ quarters. The sign of the slopes in each of the $4$ quarters are easily deduced by considering the behavior of the solution curves in these regions. This information is summarized in the following table:\n\n| $y>-1$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $↗$\n\n$(+)$ | $↘$\n\n$(-)$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{3}y+{x}^{3}={x}^{3}(y+1)\n$$\n\n evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ and the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=xy-x=x(y-1)\n$$\n\n evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=1.$\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}={x}^{2}(y+1)\n$$\n\n evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1,$ but the sign of the slopes in the required regions (summarized below) do not correspond to the given slope field.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
